    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds nice in theory but it feels totally fake. like, it's easy to say \"just be present\" when you're talking about a hobby, but when your entire identity is built on being talented... there's nothing left. i feel like i'm just rotting in place. if i can't be something extraordinary, i'm basically just taking up space.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly painful to feel like taking up space without talent is a waste, because years of hard-won value have been built on that belief system to anchor your existence. However, true presence means owning that ordinary space as your own rather than trying to force a derivative version of greatness that feels impossible; if you are not good at something, the point is simply to stop the narrative where you must be excellent to be worthy.",
      "source": "target",
